      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAIU standard KVM uses `vcpu-\u003earch.xss` to track guest xss and sets it in kvm_set_msr_common (same for cpu-\u003earch.xcr0 and __kvm_set_xcr). For pKVM we started using it with this patch to cache HW values of those regs set by host. If so, here in pkvm_restore_host_xsave_state we are changing the hw state too and therefore updating cached values as well.\n\nIf we omit `hvcpu-\u003earch.xcr0 \u003d kvm_host.xcr0;` and `hvcpu-\u003earch.ia32_xss \u003d kvm_host.xss;` here it would be probably ok too. Please also note that later in `kvm_load_host_xsave_state` restores those values to safe and default kvm_host.xss (assuming that guest xcr/xss is different than default kvm_host ones). But if we omit updating `hvcpu-\u003earch.xcr0/xss` on next  vCPU run we will still hit `hvcpu-\u003earch.xcr0 !\u003d kvm_host.xcr0` even if the host don\u0027t modify them again.\n\n\u003e ... instead we need to restore xcr0 and MSR_IA32_XSS with the hvcpu-\u003earch.xcr0 and hvcpu-\u003earch.ia32_xss before switch back to the host\n\nTaking into account that well behaving host shouldn\u0027t change HW xcr0/xss to different values than default safe kvm_host.xcr0/xss, we rather should not do that. Otherwise if we write host\u0027s tampered, restricted xcr0/xss and apply it to HW, on the exit the hyp will crash: I mean when XRSTORS will try to load Host\u0027s FPU state from memory and detect that features enabled in the XSAVE header are disabled in XCR0/XSS will trigger #GP.\n\nSo AFAIU it, well behaving host shouldn\u0027t change the hw xcr0 and xss in the first place: if for some reason it changes it we need to detect it and overwrite it back to default safe kvm_host.xcr0/xss values before switching to guest and not necessarily restore them back to those untrusted values before switching to the host. With that being said, perhaps we should not allow the host to change the hw xcr0 and xss at runtime (guard it in handle_write_msr and handle_xsetbv or print some warn)?",
